// No implicit numeric widening at a call, matching every other typed boundary (a binding, a return,
// a list element) and Rust: an `int` is not accepted where a `float` is expected. Write `sqrt(4.0)`,
// not `sqrt(4)`. The rejected call is on line 7, column 6.
// expect: error E0007 at 7:6
// expect: exit 1
use std.{math};
echo math.sqrt(4);
